<pdd-reason>The only module that reads the environment. Typed, validated, fail-fast settings built on the DEFAULT_* fallbacks from shared/constants.py.</pdd-reason>

<pdd-interface>
{"type":"module","module":{"functions":[
  {"name":"Settings","signature":"class Settings(BaseSettings)","returns":"frozen, validated settings model"},
  {"name":"settings","signature":"settings: Final[Settings]","returns":"the single module-level instance"}
]}}
</pdd-interface>

<pdd-dependency>prompts/shared/constants_python.prompt</pdd-dependency>

Implement `shared/config.py` with `pydantic_settings.BaseSettings`, reading `.env` then the
process environment.

<responsibility>
Read, type, validate, and freeze every runtime setting exactly once at import.
</responsibility>

<non_responsibilities>
This module DOES NOT declare constants — enums, key names, and `DEFAULT_*` values are imported
from `shared/constants.py` and MUST NOT be restated here.
This module DOES NOT construct Supabase, Redis, or LLM clients; `backend/deps.py` owns that.
</non_responsibilities>

<vocabulary>
**Secret** — `SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY`, `LLM_API_KEY`, `RENDER_WEBHOOK_SECRET`, `RENDER_API_KEY`.
**Required** — absence is a startup failure, not a fallback.
</vocabulary>

<capabilities>
- MAY read `.env` and `os.environ`, once, at import.
- MUST NOT perform network or database I/O.
- MUST NOT write to `.env` or any file.
</capabilities>

Settings, by group. Required keys have no default and MUST NOT be given one:

| Key | Type | Required | Fallback |
|---|---|---|---|
| `SUPABASE_URL` | `str` | yes | — |
| `SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY` | `SecretStr` | yes | — |
| `REDIS_URL` | `str` | yes | — |
| `LLM_BASE_URL` | `str` | yes | — |
| `LLM_API_KEY` | `SecretStr` | yes | — |
| `TARGET_PROMPT_DIR` | `Path` | yes | — |
| `COMPILE_COMMAND` | `str` | yes | — |
| `RENDER_WEBHOOK_SECRET` | `SecretStr` | yes | — |
| `SANDBOX_ALLOWED_HOSTS` | `tuple[str, ...]` | yes | — |
| `FORUM_ORIGIN` | `str` | yes | — |
| `SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET` | `SecretStr \| None` | no | `None` |
| `RENDER_API_KEY` | `SecretStr \| None` | no | `None` |
| `RENDER_SERVICE_ID` | `str \| None` | no | `None` |
| `DEV_MODE` | `bool` | no | `False` |
| `PITCH_COIN_LIMIT` | `int` | no | `DEFAULT_PITCH_COIN_LIMIT` |
| `UPVOTE_THRESHOLD` | `int` | no | `DEFAULT_UPVOTE_THRESHOLD` |
| `SPRINT_CADENCE_SECONDS` | `int` | no | `DEFAULT_SPRINT_CADENCE_SECONDS` |
| `MAX_RETRIES` | `int` | no | `DEFAULT_MAX_RETRIES` |
| `PENDING_PITCH_TTL_SECONDS` | `int` | no | `DEFAULT_PENDING_PITCH_TTL_SECONDS` |

<contract_rules>
R1 (MUST): Fail at import when a required key is absent, in one error naming every missing key —
not the first one only.
R2 (MUST): Take optional fallbacks from the `DEFAULT_*` constants in `shared/constants.py`; a
literal fallback value written in this module is a defect even when it currently matches.
R3 (MUST NOT): Reveal a secret's value through `repr`, `str`, logging, exception messages, or
serialisation. Secrets are typed `SecretStr` so the default representations are already masked.
R4 (MUST): Expose `settings` as a frozen instance — mutation after import raises.
R5 (MUST): Parse `SANDBOX_ALLOWED_HOSTS` from a comma-separated string into a tuple, rejecting an
empty result, since an empty allow-list would silently permit nothing (US-10).
R6 (MUST): Default `DEV_MODE` to `False`, so an unset environment enforces JWT verification. When
true the caller id comes from the `X-Dev-User` header with no verification — spoofable by design.
R7 (MUST): Reject a non-positive `PITCH_COIN_LIMIT`, `UPVOTE_THRESHOLD`, `SPRINT_CADENCE_SECONDS`,
`MAX_RETRIES`, or `PENDING_PITCH_TTL_SECONDS` at import rather than at first use.
R8 (MUST): Require `SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET` when `DEV_MODE` is false, failing at import with the
other missing keys. It is optional only because `DEV_MODE=true` skips verification entirely — an
unset secret with verification switched on would fail on the first authenticated request instead
of at startup, which is the failure this module exists to prevent (`main.py` R7).
R9 (MUST): Treat `FORUM_ORIGIN` as a single exact origin used to restrict CORS (`main.py` R16).
`*` MUST be rejected: writes carry a bearer token, so a wildcard origin is not a valid
configuration even in development.
R10 (MUST): Annotate `SANDBOX_ALLOWED_HOSTS` as `Annotated[tuple[str, ...], NoDecode]` (importing
`NoDecode` from `pydantic_settings`) so the raw environment string reaches the `mode="before"`
validator in R5. Without it pydantic-settings JSON-decodes any complex-typed field before
validation, so a comma-separated value raises `SettingsError` at import and R5's parser never
runs — the setting is unreadable in every environment, including production.
</contract_rules>

`SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY` is the service-role key: `schema.sql` relies on the service role bypassing
grants and RLS. The anon key is frontend-only and MUST NOT appear here.

<dependencies>
<include optional>shared/constants.py</include>
</dependencies>

